  "notes": [
    "[GENERAL] Assam black tea is typically brewed using freshly boiled water at 205°F to 212°F (96°C to 100°C) with a steeping time of 3 to 5 minutes.",
    "[GENERAL] A standard brewing ratio for loose-leaf black tea is approximately 2 to 3 grams (about 1 teaspoon) of leaves per 8 ounces (240 ml) of water.",
    "[GENERAL] Banaspaty is an organic tea estate located near the Karbi Anglong hills in northeast India, known for producing full-bodied, single-estate Assam orthodox teas.",
    "[GENERAL] Assam tea is crafted from the indigenous broad-leaf variety *Camellia sinensis* var. *assamica*, which naturally yields a stronger, more assertive cup than the smaller-leaf *sinensis* variety.",
    "[GENERAL] The deep malt character and brisk finish of bold Assam tea make it particularly well-suited for pairing with a splash of milk or a sweetener."
